WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.348
Hi, I'm Tango!

00:00:02.348 --> 00:00:07.288
Here's how vLLM tunes serving for a two point four trillion parameter hybrid model.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:14.309
The key: on a hybrid model, the linear layers' fixed state sets

00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:15.855
the attention layers' page size.

00:00:20.258 --> 00:00:21.601
An eight-thousand-token prompt arrives.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:25.294
Prefill engines read it all at once and build its cache.

00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:27.966
The cache moves to separate decode engines.

00:00:27.966 --> 00:00:31.182
The hand-off needs the same block size on both sides.

00:00:31.602 --> 00:00:34.167
Decode writes the answer, one token per step.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:40.410
Sixty-nine gated DeltaNet layers, twenty-three full-attention layers, and one block size

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:42.049
that must hold either.

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:46.166
DeltaNet keeps one fixed state per request, however long the prompt.

00:00:46.586 --> 00:00:48.500
Full attention grows token by token.

00:00:50.022 --> 00:00:53.916
One state equals two thousand one hundred and eight tokens; rounded to

00:00:53.916 --> 00:00:57.161
sixteen, a block is two thousand one hundred and twelve.

00:00:58.717 --> 00:01:01.837
Walk the memory ladder the server prints at startup.

00:01:01.837 --> 00:01:05.998
Sharded one way, an engine caches a hundred and twelve requests; sharded

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:07.731
wider, a hundred and eighty.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:12.129
Check the CUDA graph estimate, because it's charged to your cache.

00:01:12.549 --> 00:01:16.306
Benchmark prefill and decode apart, then combine only the winners.

00:01:16.726 --> 00:01:18.664
Find where speculation stops paying.

00:01:18.664 --> 00:01:22.927
Two doublings past two fifty-six, it costs sixty-two percent of throughput.

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:27.933
The post's own decode sweep: eight setups, speculation on and off.

00:01:28.353 --> 00:01:30.845
Solid red is speculation on eight GPUs.

00:01:30.845 --> 00:01:33.338
It peaks at two fifty-six, then falls.

00:01:33.758 --> 00:01:37.758
Only solid blue, the setup holding the most cache, keeps climbing with it on.

00:01:39.017 --> 00:01:42.435
On a hybrid model, price the linear layers first: they set the

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.999
block size and a fixed share of every request.

00:01:47.775 --> 00:01:51.155
To recap: price the cache, let the linear layers set the block,

00:01:51.155 --> 00:01:52.282
tune each phase alone.

00:01:52.702 --> 00:01:54.706
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:54.706 --> 00:01:55.279
I'm Tango.

00:01:55.279 --> 00:01:55.565
Bye!
